 ## Background
-Far-field culling was introduced in the paper "Lipschitz Pruning: Hierarchical Simplification of Primitive‐Based SDFs" [S1]. The method takes inspiration from narrow-band optimization commonly used in discrete SDF rendering [Eva15, Aal18, Söd21, SEAM22] [S1]. It is part of a broader effort to optimize SDF evaluation for complex scenes, enabling real-time rendering with ambient occlusion, shadow rays, and anti-aliasing [S1]. The method is applicable in contexts where the SDF needs to be discretized over a finite domain, such as meshing purposes [S1].
